---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../../consts';

const contactEmail = 'simsanghyeon00@gmail.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${SITE_TITLE} Clips for Slack - Privacy Policy`}
  description="Privacy Policy for Half to Full Clips for Slack."
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Half to Full Clips for Slack</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: April 28, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how Half to Full Clips for Slack ("the app")
      handles data when you install or use the app with a Slack workspace.
    </p>

    <h2>Data we collect</h2>
    <p>The app collects and stores the minimum Slack data needed to send Clip notifications:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Slack workspace ID and workspace name.</li>
      <li>The Slack channel ID and channel name selected during installation.</li>
      <li>The incoming webhook URL issued by Slack for the selected channel.</li>
      <li>The installation timestamp.</li>
      <li>A temporary OAuth state cookie used to protect the installation flow.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you contact support, we also receive the information you choose to
      include in your email, such as your email address, workspace name, and the
      details of your request.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app does not collect Slack messages, files, conversation history,
      private channel contents, user profile data, user email addresses, or
      payment information.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use data</h2>
    <p>We use the collected data to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Complete the Slack OAuth installation flow.</li>
      <li>Send new Half to Full Clip notifications to the selected Slack channel.</li>
      <li>Maintain, secure, troubleshoot, and support the app.</li>
      <li>Remove invalid installations when Slack indicates a webhook or workspace is no longer available.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data storage and retention</h2>
    <p>
      Installation records are stored with Netlify Blobs. We keep installation
      data while the app is installed, until you request deletion, until Slack
      indicates that the webhook or workspace is no longer available, or until
      the data is no longer needed to operate the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      The temporary OAuth state cookie expires after 10 minutes. Hosting and
      security logs may be processed by Netlify and retained according to
      Netlify's operational practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing and subprocessors</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell Slack data. Data may be processed by service providers
      required to operate the app, including Slack for authorization and message
      delivery, and Netlify for hosting, storage, and logs.
    </p>

    <h2>AI and model training</h2>
    <p>
      The app does not use generative AI and does not use Slack data to train
      large language models or other machine learning models.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The app uses Slack OAuth state validation and HTTPS endpoints. Webhook
      URLs and Slack credentials are treated as secrets and are not intentionally
      exposed to end users or public repositories.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices and data requests</h2>
    <p>
      You can uninstall the app from your Slack workspace at any time through
      Slack's app management settings. To request access, transfer, correction,
      or deletion of data associated with an installation, contact
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. Please include the
      Slack workspace name or workspace ID so we can identify the installation.
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      The app is operated from South Korea and may use service providers that
      process data in other countries. By installing the app, you understand
      that data may be processed where these providers operate.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy when the app changes or legal
      requirements change. The updated date above will reflect the latest
      version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or requests, email
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .updated {
    color: rgb(var(--gray));
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
